From: OpenWrt Airoha bring-up <openwrt@airoha>
Subject: [PATCH] libbpf: provide __u128/__s128 in include/linux/types.h

Kernel 7.3's arch/arm64 UAPI sigcontext.h uses __u128 (6.18 used
__uint128_t, which needs no typedef). With -I../include in the flags,
linux/types.h resolves to this compat shim, which lacked the typedefs,
breaking any TU including <signal.h> on aarch64+glibc.

Mirror the kernel UAPI definitions, guarded by __SIZEOF_INT128__.

Signed-off-by: OpenWrt Airoha bring-up <openwrt@airoha>
---
 include/linux/types.h | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

--- a/include/linux/types.h
+++ b/include/linux/types.h
@@ -22,6 +22,11 @@
 typedef __u64 __bitwise __le64;
 typedef __u64 __bitwise __be64;
 
+#ifdef __SIZEOF_INT128__
+typedef __signed__ __int128 __s128 __attribute__((aligned(16)));
+typedef unsigned __int128 __u128 __attribute__((aligned(16)));
+#endif
+
 #ifndef __aligned_u64
 # define __aligned_u64 __u64 __attribute__((aligned(8)))
 #endif
